  {
    "sha": "62815c223b61df28094bf0cb8f09d3be54624486",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVyylVtoAKDYyODE1YzIyM2I2MWRmMjgwOTRiZjBjYjhmMDlkM2JlNTQ2MjQ0ODY",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-18T16:47:08Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-18T16:47:08Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(motion): record the router example program; harden the tab fit\n\nSecond review of 613ba4abf:\n\n- B1: examples/first-router-part.nc is recorded again with\n  camcraft-cli process. Only the 2D Contour1 tab-gap lines change\n  (lines 116-148): the wider windows that the tab fit makes for the\n  Arc r3 leads. The G73 line stays as main recorded it (#2560).\n- A NaN bridge distance now counts as short, so the window grows or\n  the fit ends with the no_fit note.\n- If count * (W + D) is at least the loop length, the fit gives the\n  fill note before it reserves one entry for each tab. The app and MCP\n  do not limit the count.\n- The fixtures of contour_tab_bridge.rs that fit assert one cut run\n  between each two tabs, so they cannot pass through the fill path. A\n  new test pins the huge-count path.\n- The decision file records the known limit N2: the fit compares only\n  neighbouring cuts within W + D of each walk end.\n\nRefs #2480\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "7c807c41ff79044c280b3070f96ed7a07bb0f3cb",
